{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793515186,"nonce":"L4McdSPLnhalj8HKOkA+f34irvs=","message":"Where a kernel's first compile goes (Mac arm64, release, warm-up off).\n\nmethod_call's static-hot lua$chunk: 766 blocks lowered, 503 after optimisation (208 calls left: each guarded method site keeps its slow path), 2472 Cranelift instructions. First-call compile 27.1 ms: body 20.7, Cranelift 5.6. The pipeline ran five rounds; rounds 2 to 4 changed 14 folds + 25 merges, then 1 + 1, then nothing, and cost 2.8, 2.2 and 2.0 ms. A sample of 200 repeats of the body's pipeline: error_flag 13%, inline 12%, cse 10.5%, licm 10%, phi_prune 7.5%, sign_fold 7%, heap_scalarize 7%, drop_insert 7%; rebuild_cfg_edges 7% across cse, phi_prune, error_flag, branch_fold, inline and bounds_version; malloc and free about 10%, hash inserts 17% inclusive. No pass dominates: the cost is each pass's fixed work per round (its own maps of defs, uses and edges, `successors` returning a fresh Vec, its own rebuild_cfg_edges) over a large body.\n\n1c401628ce609aa90a8e25cb7e89d56bb6add562: non_zero and non_negative start from the values their rules can keep instead of every instruction result. Instructions per repeat of the hot functions' pipeline: method_call -2%, nbody -3.7%. Output identical: HIR dumps of every function over the 17 Lua benchmarks and 14 official files match (4161 files; the only differences are LLVM promotions, which follow timing).\n\nTried and dropped:\n- inline's caller-side cold and loop block sets made lazy: no gain, some callee always reaches the cold check.\n- an order-insensitive key for DominatorTree::of: 29 of 50 lookups hit already; 4 misses are predecessor reorderings.\n- the allocator: 3bdfe63 (macOS malloc is about a tenth of these instructions; mimalloc measured).\n\nSmall rows, any_field warm (instructions, now printed by every phase trace, f597e572fcb3fb1e8de4f3438be1712369619ee7): before main 24.0M, parse 5.7M, runtime + register 7.1M, lowering 23.4M (builtins import 9.3M, lower_program 13.0M), names + reach 2.0M, codegen registration 2.9M, placement and declarations 10.9M, run 19.1M (the kernel's first compile about 1 ms); 96M in all. Lazy stubs: 6 per run on any_field, 1 on fib. A first run after a build counts 60M more, in page faults reading the binary.","files":null}]}